      "description": "Director of Residence Life and Community Standards - HigherEdJobs Your Privacy We use cookies and other similar technologies to enhance user experience, for website maintenance purposes, and to analyze performance and traffic on our website. We also share information about your use of our website with advertising and analytics partners. If we have detected an opt-out preference signal, then it will be honored. Further information is available in our Privacy Policy . Do Not Sell My Personal Information I understand Skip to main content Sign Up | Log In Log In Sign Up Job Search By Category Administrative Faculty Executive By Location Metro/Region State/Province Country Online/Remote By School Four-Year Institutions Two-Year Institutions All Institutions Institutional Profiles By Type Dual Career Today's Jobs Adjunct/Part-Time Inclusive Workplace Military-Friendly Advanced Search My Account Signed out Account Home Job Alerts Resume/CV Other Documents My Jobs Organizer Profile Account Settings News & Resources News Advice & News Higher Ed Careers Author in Residence Ask the Expert Newsletters HigherEdJobs Podcast Resources Career Resources Job Search Tips Resume/CV Writing Service Workplace Inclusion Search Firms Employers Home Login Create Account Job Postings Post a Single Job Job Packs Unlimited Postings VIP Positions Automated Postings Other Products Digital Advertising Resume Database Institutional Profile Interim Search View All Products Posting Upgrades Inclusive Workplace Upgrade Inclusive Workplace Spotlight Priority Job Upgrade Military Upgrade Social Media Upgrade Featured Executive Position More Info Our Audience Testimonials Pay Your Invoice Contact Us Home Jobs Institution Job Listings Job Detail Director of Residence Life and Community Standards Centenary University in Hackettstown, NJ Apply Now Type: Full-Time Salary: $58,000 - $65,000 per year Posted: 6 days ago (Reposted Job: Initially posted on 09/09/2026) Application Due: 10/30/2026 Category: Residence Life and Housing ; +1 Student Affairs and Services The Director of Residence Life and Community Standards is a fulltime 12-month position that lives in college housing to provide oversight and management of the college residential populations as well as response in the event of emergencies. The Director will provide overall leadership and development of the Office of Residence Life. The Director will be responsible for the following tasks: This role has direct responsibility for housing 500 undergraduate students and a cohort of 100 Sussex residential students in eight residence halls. Under the administrative direction of the Vice President for Campus Life and Dean of Students, this educator and administrator provides visionary leadership and direction for the department; administers and manages the student housing program for the college; directs departmental operations; oversees the department budget; sets department goals; coordinates assessment efforts; and establishes learning outcomes and implementation strategies for the department. This position will collaborate and partner with many offices on campus including Security, Facilities, Information Technology, Admissions, Health and Counseling Services and other student affairs units as well as Sussex County Community College. General Responsibilities: Recruit, select and manage a staff of professionals, including an Associate Director and Graduate Resident Directors, and provide supervisory oversight for 25 RAs. Oversee the management, operation and services for the residence halls. Monitor residential life budgets and follow budget policies and practices. Maintain accurate statistics for forecasting occupancy. Work close with staff on check in procedures for early arrivals and new students to the university. Oversee the student disciplinary process so there is consistency and to ensure that we are following policies. Oversee the Student Handbook and its revision process. Oversee judicial affairs including adjudication of policy violations and tracking and identifying trends and make appropriate recommendations for their remedy. Develop and manage the residential life programming and community development agenda. Provide leadership for the planning and development of learning communities and academic initiatives within the residence halls. Develop a strong training program for all levels of staff. Update and maintain all training manuals. Maintain accurate housing and residential life policies and procedures. Update website and all marketing materials. Work close with assignment staff to coordinate continuing student housing selection process. Oversee emergency operations. Maintain an on call schedule for staff. Work closely with facilities in the maintenance of our buildings and develop capital project initiative to make improvements. Implement an office wide assessment plan on student learning, engagement/retention, and satisfaction of services. Develop new initiatives to recruit more students to live on campus. Participate in college wide committees when necessary. Emergency Response/Conflict · Remain available to students who have concerns and problems; be prepared to intervene in a crisis situation by being able to define an emergency, respond appropriately, and discern when additional professional staff, outside authorities, and the Vice President for Student Life and Dean of Students should be called for support · Meet with students or guests in residence hall who have had a detrimental effect on the College community; act as a first-level hearing officer · Communicate the institutional policies, procedures and regulations to students in the residence hall. · Be familiar with established emergency protocols and be prepared to implement them when necessary. · Remain knowledgeable of community and campus resources for referral of emotional or health problems in the residence. Aid students in decision-making concerning personal and campus issues (room changes, health, financial aid, registration). Serve as an on-call emergency responder including providing support of the responding RD as well as parental notifications and hospital transports. Other duties as assigned Communication: · Communicate with all parents and guardians regarding concerns brought to the attention of the department. · Serve as the liaison for the department staff and other administration · Provide publications and information to Campus community, residents, staff and outside community. · Work to establish positive working collaborations with other campus offices to improve the overall quality of life on campus through campus programming and initiatives. · Approve all disseminated information sent from the Department of Residence Life. Qualifications: A master's degree in higher education administration and student affairs, behavioral or social sciences, counseling, or a related discipline preferred. 3-5 years of experience in planning and managing all aspects of housing and residential life. The person in this position should have strong collaboration skills and a proven ability to build bridges and maintain successful relationships across the campus and in the community. A proven record in working with faculty in building an academic learning community that contributes to student success. Strong administrative skills and prior supervisory experience. Ability to embrace diversity and function in a fast-paced environment. Excellent interpersonal communication and writing skills. The ability to anticipate problems, reconcile conflicts, and maintain a strong philosophical base for housing and residential life. Centenary University is a learning community comprised of multifaceted and complex differences and we welcome all. We offer a supportive environment that promotes acceptance, a culture of service, skills of critical thought, and purposeful action. We are responsible for the efforts needed to create the change we seek. Equal Employment Opportunity has been, and will continue to be, a fundamental principle at Centenary University where employment is based upon personal capabilities and qualifications without discrimination because of race, color, religion, sex, age, national or ethnic origin, sexual orientation, marital status, service in Armed Forces, disability or any other protected characteristic as established by law. This policy of Equal Employment Opportunity applies to policies and procedures relating to recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, termination and other terms and conditions of employment. Apply Now Related Searches: Residence Life and Housing Student Affairs and Services Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Email: Kerry.mullins@centenaryuniversity.edu OR Apply through HigherEdJobs Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Email Your Name Message Insider Update Sign me up for the Insider Update , HigherEdJobs' newsletter for career-focused higher education professionals. Privacy Policy Insider Career Track: -- Select a Career Track -- Student Faculty Member (Tenured) Faculty Member (Non-Tenured) Post Doctorat